# sig-frx runtime dependencies.
#
# Pulled from the Fractalyze package index alongside upstream PyPI:
#   pip install -r requirements.in \
#     --extra-index-url https://fractalyze.github.io/pypi/simple/
#
# hash-frx — the symmetric layer every scheme here hashes through — is absent on
# purpose: it is a Bazel module, pinned by commit in //MODULE.bazel, not a wheel.
#
# The frx build is pinned to the one hash-frx pins, and the two must move
# together: hash-frx resolves frx from its own lock, so skew puts two different
# frx copies on one test's sys.path. zk_dtypes (native finite-field dtypes)
# arrives via frx but is pinned here directly — the frx extension-field lowering
# reads `efinfo.modulus_low_coeffs` (zk_dtypes >= 0.0.6), and this frx build
# registers the binary-field dtypes (tower t0..t7 + flat GHASH) in the frontend,
# which requires zk_dtypes >= 0.0.10.
absl-py
numpy
